The clock-lock half of E3 couldn't be run on the rented B200. The ALU-slack ladder I ran instead found the SM side has plenty of spare capacity. H15's SM-clock part looks refuted. Its L2-clock part is untested. The one-MUFU variant is slower at the unlocked clock. I'm returning r1 with the evict_last policy as a constant, which ties r1.

